[Better Approach] Reverse Preorder - O(n) Time and O(h) SpaceThe idea is to process the tree in reverse preorder: Right -> Left -> Root, so that when we process a node, its next node in the required preorder list is already available in prev. We then connect root-> right to prev and set root-> left = null, gradually building the flattened list in Root -> Left -> Right order.If root is null, return the previously processed node prev.Recursively process the right subtree first and update prev. Recursively process the left subtree and update prev. Set root->right = prev and make root->left = null. Update prev = root and return it. This reverse preorder processing builds the flattened tree in preorder: Root -> Left -> Right.
