[Expected Approach] Morris Traversal - O(n) Time and O(1) SpaceThe idea is to use Morris Traversal to flatten the tree in-place without recursion or a stack. For each node with a left subtree, we connect the original right subtree to the rightmost node of the left subtree, then move the left subtree to the right, maintaining the Root -> Left -> Right preorder order while using O(1) extra space.Start from the root and process each node while curr != null.If curr has no left child, simply move to curr->right. Otherwise, find the rightmost node of curr's left subtree. Connect this rightmost node to curr->right (the original right subtree). Move the left subtree to curr->right and set curr->left = null. Move to curr->right and repeat until the entire tree is flattened.
